  "body": "I attempted to extract the IDL sections from the spec and process them to obtain a list of global object names. However parsing one `<pre class=\"idl…` failed, namely in the section [APIs for the text control selections](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#textFieldSelection):\n\n> The `input` and `textarea` elements define the following members in their\n>   DOM interfaces for handling their selection:\n> \n> ```\n>   void select();\n>   attribute unsigned long? selectionStart;\n>   attribute unsigned long? selectionEnd;\n>   attribute DOMString? selectionDirection;\n>   void setRangeText(DOMString replacement);\n>   void setRangeText(DOMString replacement, unsigned long start, unsigned long end, optional SelectionMode selectionMode = \"preserve\");\n>   void setSelectionRange(unsigned long start, unsigned long end, optional DOMString direction = \"preserve\");\n> ```\n\nAs far as I understand it, this is only an IDL _snippet_, not a complete [IDL _fragment_](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#dfn-idl-fragment) since it is not a top level definition. Perhaps it would be possible to encapsulate these methods into some `[NoInterfaceObject]` interface definition, to comply with the Web IDL spec for all the IDL sections?\n",
